<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<xmile version="1.0" level="3" xmlns="http://www.systemdynamics.org/XMILE" xmlns:isee="http://iseesystems.com/XMILE">
    <header>
        <smile version="1.0" namespace="std, isee">
            <uses_arrays>1</uses_arrays>
        </smile>
        <name>Traffic.v5</name>
        <uuid>f30a4f9c-5c28-4822-ad2d-766e6c54c1f9</uuid>
        <vendor>isee systems, inc.</vendor>
        <product version="10.1.2" isee:saved_by_v1="false" lang="en">iThink</product>
    </header>
    <style>
        <model font-family="Arial" font-size="12" />
        <interface font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
    </style>
    <sim_specs method="RK4" time_units="Years" isee:pause_after_rates="false" isee:instantaneous_flows="false">
        <start>1990</start>
        <stop>2040</stop>
        <dt>0.1</dt>
        <isee:analyze_mode>false</isee:analyze_mode>
    </sim_specs>
    <dimensions>
        <dim name="Dim_Name_1">
            <elem name="Element_1" />
        </dim>
        <dim name="Counties">
            <elem name="Multnomah" />
            <elem name="Clackamas" />
            <elem name="Washington" />
        </dim>
        <dim name="Dim_Name_3" size="1" />
        <dim name="Dim_Name_4" size="1" />
        <dim name="Dim_Name_5" size="1" />
    </dimensions>
    <model_units />
    <isee:prefs last_model="true" layer="model" grid_width="20" grid_height="50" divide_by_zero_alert="true" link_high_level_map="true" show_module_prefix="true">
        <isee:window width="806" height="568" />
        <isee:security />
        <isee:print_setup width="552" height="728" />
    </isee:prefs>
    <isee:equation_prefs order_by="sector" show_documentation="true" show_pages="true" />
    <model>
        <stock name="East_Side_Light_Rail_Riders">
            <doc>This is the total number of people who ride light rail. This number was found at the Theano Institutes web site.</doc>
            <eqn>26000 {People}</eqn>
            <inflow>Change_in_Riders</inflow>
            <display x="730" y="625" color="white" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Change_in_Riders">
            <doc>This is the change in the number of light rail riders each year.  The reason we subtracted East Side Light Rail in this equation is because they would have been calculated twice.</doc>
            <eqn>(Number_of_Commuters*Percent_that_ride_light_rail)-East_Side_Light_Rail_Riders {People per year}</eqn>
            <display x="644" y="624" color="white">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="578" y="624" />
                    <pt x="710" y="624" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Percent_that_ride_light_rail">
            <doc>This is the percent of commuters that ride light rail. It is determined by multiplying the light rail multiplier by the initial (1990) percent that ride light rail.</doc>
            <eqn>Effect_of_Average_Commuting_Time_on_Percent_that_ride_Light_Rail*Init_Percent_ride_light_rail {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="746" y="685" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Init_Percent_ride_light_rail">
            <doc>This is the percent of commuters that ride light rail in 1990. This number was found at the Theano institutes website.</doc>
            <eqn>.046 {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="615" y="685" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Effect_of_Average_Commuting_Time_on_Percent_that_ride_Light_Rail">
            <doc>This graph affects the percent of commuters that ride light rail. As the average car commuting time goes up, the percent that ride light rail go up. As the average car commuting time goes down, the percent that ride light rail goes down.</doc>
            <eqn>Average_Car_Commuting_Time {No Units}</eqn>
            <gf>
                <xscale min="0" max="50" />
                <yscale min="0.7" max="1.3" />
                <ypts>0.69999999999999996,0.84099999999999997,0.93099999999999994,0.99099999999999999,1.018,1.0329999999999999,1.0509999999999999,1.0720000000000001,1.123,1.1890000000000001,1.3</ypts>
            </gf>
            <display x="940" y="661" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <stock name="Metro_Population">
            <doc>This is the total number of people in the Portland Metro area. The number that starts in this stock is the number of people in the Metro area in 1990. This number was found in the Metro green book.</doc>
            <eqn>1174291 {People}</eqn>
            <inflow>Change_in_Metro_Population</inflow>
            <display x="177" y="119" color="black" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Change_in_Metro_Population">
            <doc>This is the change in the Metro population. It is a biflow, which means that the population can go up or down. The change in Metro population is determined by multiplying the Metro population by the Metro growth rate.</doc>
            <eqn>Metro_Population*Metro_Growth_Rate {People per year}</eqn>
            <display x="95" y="121" color="black">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="34" y="121" />
                    <pt x="157" y="121" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Metro_Initial_Growth_Rate">
            <doc>This is the initial (1990) rate of growth for the Metro area taken from the Metro Regional Data Book. It is used to determine the current growth rate for the Metro area.</doc>
            <eqn>.03657 {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="69" y="261" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Metro_Growth_Rate">
            <doc>This is the rate at which the Metro population grows. It is determined by multiplying the initial growth rate by the effect of Metro Density on Metro growth rate.</doc>
            <eqn>Metro_Initial_Growth_Rate*Effect_of_Metro_Density_on_Metro_Growth_Rate {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="134" y="205" color="black" label_angle="283" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Land_in_Metro_Growth_Boundry">
            <doc>This is the total number of square miles in the Metro area. This number was found in the Metro green book.</doc>
            <eqn>461.8 {Sq. Miles}</eqn>
            <display x="330" y="204" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Initial_Density">
            <doc>This is the initial (1990) density in the metro area. Density is defined as the number of people per square mile. It is used to determine how much more dense the Metro area will become.</doc>
            <eqn>(INIT(Metro_Population))/Land_in_Metro_Growth_Boundry {People per sq. mile}</eqn>
            <display x="317" y="273" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Current_Density">
            <doc>This is the current number of people per square mile in the Metro area. It is compared to the initial (1990) density to determine how much more dense the Metro area will become in the future.</doc>
            <eqn>Metro_Population/Land_in_Metro_Growth_Boundry {People per sq. Mile}</eqn>
            <display x="265" y="144" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Number_of_Commuters">
            <doc>This is the total number of commuters in the Metro area. This number is determined by mulplying the percent commuters by the Metro population.</doc>
            <eqn>Percent_Commuters*Metro_Population {Peoples}</eqn>
            <display x="490" y="223" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Current_Vs_Initial_Density">
            <doc>This is the current vs initial density. It is used to determine by how much the density will increase. </doc>
            <eqn>Current_Density/Initial_Density {No Units}</eqn>
            <display x="215" y="307" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Effect_of_Metro_Density_on_Metro_Growth_Rate">
            <doc>This is a graph that is based on the Current vs. Initial density. As the current vs initial density goes up, the graph goes down. If the current vs initial density goes down, the graph goes up. This graph can be multiplied by the initial metro growth to determine the current growth rate.</doc>
            <eqn>Current_Vs_Initial_Density {No Units}</eqn>
            <gf>
                <xscale min="0" max="2" />
                <yscale min="0.1" max="5" />
                <ypts>5,3.8975,2.0845000000000002,1.3740000000000001,1.129,1,0.85950000000000004,0.73699999999999999,0.59000000000000008,0.39400000000000002,0.10000000000000001</ypts>
            </gf>
            <display x="124" y="346" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Percent_Commuters">
            <doc>This is the total percent of the population that commutes to work. This number is multiplied by the Metro population to determine how many commuters are in Portland. This number was found in the Metro Green Book.</doc>
            <eqn>.475 {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="490" y="87" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <stock name="Bus_Riders">
            <doc>This is the total number of people who ride the bus in Portland. The number was found by multiplying the number of commuters by the percent that rides the bus.</doc>
            <eqn>33200 {People}</eqn>
            <inflow>Change_in_Bus_Riders</inflow>
            <display x="755" y="40" color="white" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Change_in_Bus_Riders">
            <doc>This is the change in the number of people who ride the bus. It is determined by the number of people who commute and the percent of people that ride the bus.  The reason we subtracted Bus riders in this equation is because they would have been calculated twice.</doc>
            <eqn>(Percent_Bus_Riders*Number_of_Commuters)-Bus_Riders {People per Year}</eqn>
            <display x="686" y="42" color="white" label_angle="282">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="637" y="42" />
                    <pt x="735" y="42" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Percent_Bus_Riders">
            <doc>This converter determines what percent of commuters ride the bus. It multiplies the Initial Percent Bus Riders by the Bus multiplier.</doc>
            <eqn>Effect_of_Commuting_time_on_Percent_that_ride_the_bus*Init_Percent_Bus_Riders {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="641" y="149" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <stock name="Drive_Alone">
            <doc>This is the total number of people who drive to work alone. This number was determined by multiplying the number of commuters by the percent that drive alone to work.</doc>
            <eqn>410000 {People}</eqn>
            <inflow>Change_in_Drivers</inflow>
            <display x="756" y="215" color="white" label_angle="84" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Change_in_Drivers">
            <doc>This is the change in the number of commuters who drive alone to work. It is determined by multiplying the number of commuters by the percent that drive alone.  The reason we subtracted Drive alone in this equation is because they would have been calculated twice.</doc>
            <eqn>(Number_of_Commuters*Percent_that_drive_alone)-Drive_Alone {People per Year}</eqn>
            <display x="685" y="207" color="white" label_angle="295">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="635" y="207" />
                    <pt x="736" y="207" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Percent_that_drive_alone">
            <doc>This is the current percent of commuters that drive alone. This number is determined by multiplying the Init percent by the Drivers Multiplier.</doc>
            <eqn>Init_Percent_Drive_Alone*(Effect_of_Commuting_time_on_percent_that_drive_alone) {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="649" y="275" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <stock name="Car_Poolers">
            <doc>This is the number of people who car pool. This number was determined by multiplying the number of commuters by the percent of commuters that car pool.</doc>
            <eqn>70340 {People}</eqn>
            <inflow>Change_in_Car_Poolers</inflow>
            <display x="757" y="416" color="white" label_angle="99" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Change_in_Car_Poolers">
            <doc>This is the change in the number of car poolers.  The reason we subtracted Car Poolers in this equation is because they would have been calculated twice.</doc>
            <eqn>(Number_of_Commuters*Percent_Car_Poolers)-Car_Poolers {People per Year}</eqn>
            <display x="687" y="418" color="white" label_angle="288">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="637" y="418" />
                    <pt x="737" y="418" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Percent_Car_Poolers">
            <doc>This is the percentage of commuters that car pool to work. It is determined by multipying the INIT car poolers percnet by the car pooling multiplier.</doc>
            <eqn>INIT_Car_Poolers_Percent*(Effect_of_Average_Commuting_time_on_Percent_that_car_pool) {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="786" y="527" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Lane_Miles_in_the_Metro_Area">
            <doc>This is the number of lane miles in the Metro area. We found this number in the Oregon Milage Report.</doc>
            <eqn>7183 {Lane Miles}</eqn>
            <display x="170" y="415" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Cars_per_Lane_Mile">
            <doc>This converter determines what the current traffic density is. The value is basically vehicles per lane mile. We added the number of busses and cars and divided it by the number of lane miles to determine the traffic.</doc>
            <eqn>(Busses+Cars+Cars_used_for_car_pooling)/Lane_Miles_in_the_Metro_Area {P. Vehicles per Lane Mile}&#x0D;</eqn>
            <display x="118" y="529" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Busses">
            <doc>This is the total number of busses that are carrying people. It is determined by dividing the number of people who ride the bus by the number of riders per bus.</doc>
            <eqn>Bus_Riders/Riders_per_bus {P. Vehicle}</eqn>
            <display x="901" y="25" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Riders_per_bus">
            <doc>This is the average number of riders per bus. </doc>
            <eqn>20 {People per P. Vehicle}</eqn>
            <display x="985" y="24" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Cars">
            <doc>This is the total number of cars transporting a single person.</doc>
            <eqn>Drive_Alone {P. Vehicle}</eqn>
            <display x="852" y="215" color="black" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Cars_used_for_car_pooling">
            <doc>This is the number of cars being used for car pooling. It is determined by dividing the number of car poolers by the number of people per car pool.</doc>
            <eqn>Car_Poolers/People_per_car_pool {P. Vehicle}</eqn>
            <display x="865" y="416" color="white" label_angle="260" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="People_per_car_pool">
            <doc>This is the average number of people per car pool.</doc>
            <eqn>2.5 {People per P. Vehicle}</eqn>
            <display x="954" y="384" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Init_vehicles_per_lane_mile">
            <doc>This is the initial (1990) traffic.</doc>
            <eqn>INIT(Cars_per_Lane_Mile) {P. Vehicles per Lane Mile}</eqn>
            <display x="275" y="462" color="white" label_angle="229" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Current_Vs_Init_Traffic">
            <doc>This is the current traffic vs. the initial traffic.  We use this value to determine the average commuting time.</doc>
            <eqn>Cars_per_Lane_Mile/Init_vehicles_per_lane_mile {No Units}</eqn>
            <display x="275" y="591" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Init_Percent_Drive_Alone">
            <doc>This is the percent of commuters that drove alone in 1990. This number was found in the Metro Green Book.</doc>
            <eqn>.726 {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="641" y="331" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Effect_of_Commuting_time_on_Percent_that_ride_the_bus">
            <doc>This graph determines how many people ride the bus. As the average commuting time increases the graph increases. If the average commuting time decreases, the graph decreases.</doc>
            <eqn>Average_Car_Commuting_Time {No Units}</eqn>
            <gf>
                <xscale min="0" max="50" />
                <yscale min="0.7" max="1.3" />
                <ypts>0.69999999999999996,0.84099999999999997,0.92500000000000004,0.96699999999999997,1,1.0389999999999999,1.0660000000000001,1.0960000000000001,1.141,1.198,1.3</ypts>
            </gf>
            <display x="830" y="144" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Init_Percent_Bus_Riders">
            <doc>This is the initial (1990) percent of commuters that ride the bus. This number was found in the Metro Green Book.</doc>
            <eqn>.045 {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="741" y="104" color="white" label_angle="286" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Effect_of_Commuting_time_on_percent_that_drive_alone">
            <doc>This graph alters the percent of the population that drives alone. As the average commuting time increases, this decreases the percent that drive alone. If the average commuting time decreases, this increases the percent that drive alone.</doc>
            <eqn>Average_Car_Commuting_Time {No Units}</eqn>
            <gf>
                <xscale min="0" max="50" />
                <yscale min="0.7" max="1.3" />
                <ypts>1.3,1.135,1.0720000000000001,1.036,1,0.98799999999999999,0.97599999999999998,0.94899999999999995,0.91000000000000003,0.82899999999999996,0.69999999999999996</ypts>
            </gf>
            <display x="829" y="317" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="INIT_Car_Poolers_Percent">
            <doc>This is the percent of commuters that car pooled in 1990. This number was found in the Metro Green Book.</doc>
            <eqn>.125 {1/Year}</eqn>
            <display x="648" y="500" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Average_Car_Commuting_Time">
            <doc>This is the average car commuting time. It starts out at the 1990 level and increases based on how much the traffic increases.</doc>
            <eqn>Init_Car_Commute_time*Current_Vs_Init_Traffic {Minutes}</eqn>
            <display x="424" y="560" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Init_Car_Commute_time">
            <doc>This is the average car commute in the year 1990. This number was found in the Metro Green Book.</doc>
            <eqn>20.4 {Minutes}</eqn>
            <display x="424" y="437" color="white" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="Effect_of_Average_Commuting_time_on_Percent_that_car_pool">
            <doc>This is the car pooling graph. It affects the percent of commuters that car pool to work. As the average car commuting time increases, the car pooling graph increases, which increases the percent car poolers. If the average commuting time decreases, the graph decreases, which decreases the percent that car pool.</doc>
            <eqn>Average_Car_Commuting_Time {No Units}</eqn>
            <gf>
                <xscale min="0" max="50" />
                <yscale min="0.7" max="1.3" />
                <ypts>0.69999999999999996,0.83799999999999997,0.91600000000000004,0.96699999999999997,1,1.0209999999999999,1.042,1.054,1.087,1.153,1.3</ypts>
            </gf>
            <display x="960" y="509" color="white" label_angle="257" />
        </aux>
        <display show_pages="true" page_width="552" page_height="728" page_cols="3" isee:converter_size="large" isee:animate_flows="true" isee:animate_stocks="true" isee:animate_converters="true">
            <alias x="52" y="418" uid="0" color="black">
                <of>Busses</of>
            </alias>
            <connector x="735" y="680" uid="1" color="white">
                <from>Percent_that_ride_light_rail</from>
                <to>Change_in_Riders</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="490" y="235" uid="2" color="black">
                <from>Number_of_Commuters</from>
                <to>Change_in_Riders</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="709" y="628" uid="3" color="white">
                <from>East_Side_Light_Rail_Riders</from>
                <to>Change_in_Riders</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="627" y="685" uid="4" color="white">
                <from>Init_Percent_ride_light_rail</from>
                <to>Percent_that_ride_light_rail</to>
            </connector>
            <alias x="939" y="588" uid="5">
                <of>Average_Car_Commuting_Time</of>
            </alias>
            <connector x="930" y="660" uid="6" color="white">
                <from>Effect_of_Average_Commuting_Time_on_Percent_that_ride_Light_Rail</from>
                <to>Percent_that_ride_light_rail</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="940" y="600" uid="7" color="white">
                <from>
                    <alias uid="5" />
                </from>
                <to>Effect_of_Average_Commuting_Time_on_Percent_that_ride_Light_Rail</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="155" y="130" uid="8" color="black">
                <from>Metro_Population</from>
                <to>Change_in_Metro_Population</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="128" y="195" uid="9" color="black">
                <from>Metro_Growth_Rate</from>
                <to>Change_in_Metro_Population</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="72" y="249" uid="10" color="black">
                <from>Metro_Initial_Growth_Rate</from>
                <to>Metro_Growth_Rate</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="128" y="335" uid="11" color="black">
                <from>Effect_of_Metro_Density_on_Metro_Growth_Rate</from>
                <to>Metro_Growth_Rate</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="330" y="216" uid="12" color="black">
                <from>Land_in_Metro_Growth_Boundry</from>
                <to>Initial_Density</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="328" y="192" uid="13" color="black">
                <from>Land_in_Metro_Growth_Boundry</from>
                <to>Current_Density</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="197" y="126" uid="14" color="black">
                <from>Metro_Population</from>
                <to>Current_Density</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="181" y="134" uid="15" color="black">
                <from>Metro_Population</from>
                <to>Initial_Density</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="306" y="278" uid="16" color="black">
                <from>Initial_Density</from>
                <to>Current_Vs_Initial_Density</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="729" y="106" uid="17" color="white">
                <from>Init_Percent_Bus_Riders</from>
                <to>Percent_Bus_Riders</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="818" y="144" uid="18" color="white">
                <from>Effect_of_Commuting_time_on_Percent_that_ride_the_bus</from>
                <to>Percent_Bus_Riders</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="661" y="273" uid="19" color="white">
                <from>Percent_that_drive_alone</from>
                <to>Change_in_Drivers</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="502" y="223" uid="20" color="black">
                <from>Number_of_Commuters</from>
                <to>Change_in_Drivers</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="777" y="519" uid="21" color="white">
                <from>Percent_Car_Poolers</from>
                <to>Change_in_Car_Poolers</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="494" y="234" uid="22" color="black">
                <from>Number_of_Commuters</from>
                <to>Change_in_Car_Poolers</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="494" y="212" uid="23" color="black">
                <from>Number_of_Commuters</from>
                <to>Change_in_Bus_Riders</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="734" y="218" uid="24" color="white">
                <from>Drive_Alone</from>
                <to>Change_in_Drivers</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="743" y="433" uid="25" color="white">
                <from>Car_Poolers</from>
                <to>Change_in_Car_Poolers</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="973" y="24" uid="26" color="white">
                <from>Riders_per_bus</from>
                <to>Busses</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="775" y="37" uid="27" color="white">
                <from>Bus_Riders</from>
                <to>Busses</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="776" y="215" uid="28" color="white">
                <from>Drive_Alone</from>
                <to>Cars</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="59" y="428" uid="29" color="black">
                <from>
                    <alias uid="0" />
                </from>
                <to>Cars_per_Lane_Mile</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="104" y="599" uid="31" color="black">
                <from>
                    <alias uid="30" />
                </from>
                <to>Cars_per_Lane_Mile</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="163" y="425" uid="32" color="white">
                <from>Lane_Miles_in_the_Metro_Area</from>
                <to>Cars_per_Lane_Mile</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="943" y="389" uid="33" color="white">
                <from>People_per_car_pool</from>
                <to>Cars_used_for_car_pooling</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="777" y="416" uid="34" color="white">
